      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just to add more context, this only happens with VRC_Spatial_Audio_Source has \"Enable Spatialization\" checked. With spatialization off both channels play. This, and the fact that everything works fine on the Noise build (Steam audio) points to it being something with Oculus's ONSP spatilizer, or how its being utilized.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-08-12T23:24:50.452Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, when using an UdonSyncPlayer (Unity), with a Stereo video (with a SINGLE, STEREO audio track) the right channel will be missing completely. This is a change from 2018 client. The Noise build does not have this bug. \nHow it used to work, and how it still does in the editor and noise build, is that each audio TRACK in the video would get sent to an audio source. Currently this is not the case, now each audio track is being treated as Mono (losing any extra channels in the track, like the right channel), and getting sent to the first audio source.  This means every YouTube video will have this issue as those are single track, dual channel, stereo just like my tests here.\nI tried splitting the stereo track, into two mono tracks, and mapping the video player to two audio sources, this works. However it shouldn't be necessary and you wont have the ability to do that for YouTube videos.\nThis is clearly a bug. I've attached a video showing the issue.\nhttps://youtu.be/UR-dUciQ7OQ",
